<title>UK: Argos slides on Hoare Govett downgrade.</title>
<headline>Argos slides on Hoare Govett downgrade.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Argos Plc tumbled to their lowest level since November 1995 after brokerage ABN AMRO Hoare Govett downgraded its earnings estimates for the UK retailer, dealers said.</p>
<p>At 0857 GMT, the shares were off 23p to 572-1/2 in a generally steady retail sector.  </p>
<p>The analyst said she had reduced her earnings forecast, but declined to provide details. She said she was maintaining her &quot;weak hold&quot; recommendation on the stock.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
